You have been asked to design a new set of coins. All the coins are round and the same color, and only their diameters differ. Experts think the set must meet the following requirements:

• coin diameters must be no less than 18 mm and no more than 50 mm;
• each coin's diameter must be at least 25% larger than the previous one;
• the minting machine can only produce coins whose diameters are a whole number of millimeters (for example, 23 mm is possible, 23.4 mm is not).
